  "notes": "USAGE:\nAlmost exclusively used in the pattern {命|いのち}を{取|と}り{留|と}める or {一命|いちめい}を{取|と}り{留|と}める. Rarely used with other objects.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {命|いのち}を{取|と}り{留|と}める (to survive, to have one's life saved)\n- {一命|いちめい}を{取|と}り{留|と}める (to barely survive — more formal/dramatic)\n- {何|なん}とか{命|いのち}を{取|と}り{留|と}めた (somehow managed to survive)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- とりとめのない (rambling, incoherent — a separate, common expression from the same root)\n- {九死|きゅうし}に{一生|いっしょう}を{得|え}る (to have a narrow escape from death)",
